-- title:
--   Lemma 8.4 — fidelity selection from independent Clifford shadows
-- statement:
--   Fix a density matrix $\rho$, an optimal stabilizer projector $|\phi^*\rangle\langle\phi^*|$, $\varepsilon>0$, $0<\delta<1$, and a fixed list $\mathcal C$ of stabilizer states containing $|\phi^*\rangle$, with $|\mathcal C|\le M$. Using
--   $$N_{\rm sh}=O\!\left(\frac{\ln(8M/\delta)}{\varepsilon^2}\right)$$
--   independent global-Clifford measurements (median of $2\lceil4\ln(8M/\delta)\rceil+1$ means of $\lceil48/\varepsilon^2\rceil$ records), with probability at least $1-\delta/8$
--   $$|\tilde f(\phi)-\langle\phi|\rho|\phi\rangle|\le\varepsilon/2\ \text{ for all }\phi\in\mathcal C,\qquad\langle\hat\phi|\rho|\hat\phi\rangle\ge F(\rho)-\varepsilon,$$
--   where $\hat\phi$ maximizes $\tilde f$. The $O$-constant is absolute (the count bound is stated for $0<\varepsilon\le1$).
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: an n-qubit state ρ on (ℂ²)^{⊗n} → a matrix ρ : Op (Qubits n) indexed by Boolean strings with IsDensity ρ (positive semidefinite, trace one); bits of F₂ⁿ are converted by toQubits/ofQubits; reason: the same density operators in the computational basis
--   - encoding: the label space T of a fixed optimal stabilizer state |ϕ*⟩ → labelSpace P for a projector P with IsOptimalStab ρ P (P ∈ Stab_n and tr(ρP) = F(ρ)); reason: states are compared as projectors; the span of the stabilizing labels of a stabilizer projector is its label space
--   - generalization: N_sh = O(ln(8|𝒞|/δ)/ε²) → the explicit median-of-means schedule for any bound M ≥ |𝒞|, with an absolute constant K in N_sh ≤ K ln(8M/δ)/ε²; reason: M = |𝒞| gives the source's statement; Algorithm 5 uses M = M_max
--   - reading: N_sh = O(ln(8|𝒞|/δ)/ε²) with no range of ε stated in the lemma → the count bound N_sh ≤ K ln(8M/δ)/ε² for 0 < ε ≤ 1 (the range of Theorem 1.1); the probability clause holds for every ε > 0; reason: for ε > 1 an O(1/ε²) count of at least one record is meaningless, so the O-claim refers to the paper's range ε ≤ 1
--   - generalization: 0 < δ < 1/3 (the range of Theorem 1.1) → 0 < δ < 1; reason: a larger parameter range; it specializes to the source's range
--   - encoding: uniformly random n-qubit Clifford unitary followed by a computational-basis measurement → U uniform on the group generated by H, S and CNOT (with phases), record probability |Cl|⁻¹⟨b|UρU†|b⟩; reason: this group is the n-qubit Clifford group; global phases do not affect the record law or X_ϕ
--   - generalization: conditional on the earlier measurement batches (the lists produced by the previous stages) → every fixed list (or set) satisfying the stated hypotheses, with probability over the fresh independent batch only; reason: conditioning on the earlier batches fixes these inputs; a statement for every fixed input specializes to the conditional one
-- source:
--   Ching-Yi Lai, STOC 2027 submission #1629 (October 2026), p. 36 (PDF p. 37), Lemma 8.4, equations (105)–(106)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_BatchStabilizer_Learning_Algorithms

set_option autoImplicit false
open scoped ComplexOrder BigOperators Matrix Kronecker
open LindbladTolerant.Testing

namespace BatchStabilizer.Learning

/-- Lemma 8.4, printed p. 36 (PDF p. 37): with `N_sh = O(ln(8M/δ)/ε²)` independent global-Clifford
shadow records (the median of `2⌈4 ln(8M/δ)⌉ + 1` group means of `⌈48/ε²⌉` records each, `M ≥ |𝒞|`), if the
fixed signed list `𝒞` contains the optimal state `|ϕ*⟩`, then with probability at least `1 - δ/8`
all estimates satisfy `|f̃(ϕ) - ⟨ϕ|ρ|ϕ⟩| ≤ ε/2` and the selected maximizer `ϕ̂` has
`⟨ϕ̂|ρ|ϕ̂⟩ ≥ F(ρ) - ε` (106).  The count bound is stated for `0 < ε ≤ 1`; the probability
clause for every `ε > 0`. -/
theorem lemma_8_4 :
    (∃ K : ℝ, 0 < K ∧ ∀ ε δ : ℝ, 0 < ε → ε ≤ 1 → 0 < δ → δ < 1 → ∀ M : ℕ, 1 ≤ M →
      ((shadowGroups δ M * shadowGroupSize ε : ℕ) : ℝ) ≤ K * Real.log (8 * M / δ) / ε ^ 2) ∧
    ∀ (n : ℕ) (ρ P : Op (Qubits n)), IsDensity ρ → IsOptimalStab ρ P →
      ∀ ε δ : ℝ, 0 < ε → 0 < δ → δ < 1 →
      ∀ (cands : List (Op (Qubits n))) (M : ℕ), cands.length ≤ M →
        (∀ Q ∈ cands, Q ∈ ArbLindbladLearn.Stab n) → P ∈ cands →
        1 - δ / 8 ≤
          (Prog.shadow (shadowGroups δ M * shadowGroupSize ε) (fun R => Prog.ret R) :
              Prog n (Fin (shadowGroups δ M * shadowGroupSize ε) → Op (Qubits n) × Qubits n)).prob ρ
            (fun R =>
              (∀ Q ∈ cands, |shadowEstimate (shadowGroupSize ε) (shadowGroups δ M) R Q -
                  (ρ * Q).trace.re| ≤ ε / 2) ∧
              stabFidelity ρ - ε ≤
                (ρ * selectBest cands
                  (shadowEstimate (shadowGroupSize ε) (shadowGroups δ M) R)).trace.re) := by sorry

end BatchStabilizer.Learning
